# Path classes of this project (docs/documentation-rules.md, sections 8 and 9): one
# "<class> <glob>" per line, a shell glob relative to the repository root, in which * also matches
# /. A path takes the highest class among the lines that match it and the template's built-in
# ones (approval for the rules, the map, ADRs on main, and generated files). A path that nothing
# matches is low when it is Markdown, otherwise normal. This file belongs to the project; a
# change to it is class approval.
#   approval  the owner approves the edit first: the protect hook asks, a headless run is denied
#   high      Santa loop before the pull request: two reviewers until neither finds a blocker
#   gate      listed under "Gate files" in the pull request, reviewed by the owner after the merge
#   normal    one reviewer before the pull request
#   low       no reviewer before the pull request

# Secrets and tools with irreversible effects.
approval .env
approval .env.*
approval *.pem
approval *.key

# Security, access, data migrations, money. Add the project's own, such as policy or limits.
high *auth/*
high *security/*
high *secrets/*
high *migrations/*
high *billing/*
high *payments/*

# Gates: workflows, the project's checks and Stop hooks, harness settings, dependency manifests
# and lock files, and the configuration of linters, test runners, coverage, and mutation testing.
gate .github/workflows/*
gate scripts/checks.d/*
gate .claude/hooks/project/*
gate .claude/harness.conf
gate package.json
gate */package.json
gate package-lock.json
gate pnpm-lock.yaml
gate yarn.lock
gate pyproject.toml
gate uv.lock
gate poetry.lock
gate requirements*.txt
gate go.mod
gate go.sum
gate Cargo.toml
gate Cargo.lock
gate .eslintrc*
gate eslint.config.*
gate .prettierrc*
gate ruff.toml
gate .ruff.toml
gate pytest.ini
gate tox.ini
gate .coveragerc
gate jest.config.*
gate vitest.config.*
gate tsconfig*.json
gate stryker.conf.*
gate .golangci.yml
